-- title:
--   A finite bracket for the gamma-phase limit
-- statement:
--   Let $x>0$, $y\ge0$ be real, and $n_0$ a nonnegative integer. Define
--
--   $$f(u)=\arctan\!\frac{y}{x+u},\quad
--   F(u)=(x+u)f(u)+\frac y2\log\bigl((x+u)^2+y^2\bigr),\quad
--   L_n=y\log n-\sum_{k=0}^{n}f(k).$$
--
--   Assume $L_n\to\lambda$ as $n\to\infty$, and put
--   $B=F(n_0)+f(n_0)/2-\sum_{k=0}^{n_0}f(k)-y$. Then
--
--   $$B-\frac{y}{4((x+n_0)^2+y^2)}\le\lambda\le B.$$
--
--   This provides explicit finite bounds on the phase limit.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/RSTheta.lean#L390-L420

